eve in Kaggle submission. Totally 3 diverse types of neural network operations are tried on this dataset i.e. 1) Single Hidden MLP 2) RNN 3) DNN each Neural Net is processed in different ipynb files before combining it. DNN is my baseline model because I achieved my maximum accuracy of 88.53% while processing data with it and rank achieved in it is 1335 out of 9,803.","topics":[],"score":236904,"global_rank":88976},{"name":"shik3519/deep-learning","owner":"shik3519","html_url":"https://github.com/shik3519/deep-learning","stars":3,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Jupyter Notebook","description":null,"topics":["cnn-model","dataloader","pytorch"],"score":236900,"global_rank":88980},{"name":"J-DUB64/MLNN_JHU","owner":"J-DUB64","html_url":"https://github.com/J-DUB64/MLNN_JHU","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Jupyter Notebook","description":"Johns Hopkins University MLNN Course Repository  This repository contains projects, assignments, and resources related to the Machine Learning Neural Networks (MLNN) course at Johns Hopkins University. ","topics":[],"score":236896,"global_rank":88996}]